# Dart Style, Lints, Analysis

## Required hygiene
- ✅ Run formatting before committing: `dart format .`
- ✅ Keep analyzer clean (warnings treated as errors in CI)
- ✅ Follow project analyzer config (`home_organizer_flutter_app/analysis_options.yaml`):
  - `include: package:flutter_lints/flutter.yaml`
  - `invalid_annotation_target: ignore` (required for `freezed` + `json_serializable`)
- ✅ Prefer `final` and `const`
- ✅ Use explicit types at API boundaries (public methods, DTOs)

## Imports
- ✅ Use `package:` imports for lib code
- ✅ Relative imports only within the same directory (avoid deep relative paths)
- ✅ No circular imports; use feature public API files if needed

## Types
- ✅ Avoid `dynamic`
- ✅ Avoid `late` unless lifecycle requires it
- ✅ Avoid `var` when it reduces readability

## Async
- ✅ Always `await` Futures unless intentionally fire-and-forget (comment why)
- ✅ No unhandled Future errors (use `try/catch` with typed failures)

## Codegen discipline
- ✅ Generated files stay generated; never hand-edit:
  - `*.freezed.dart`, `*.g.dart`
- ✅ Use build_runner commands (examples):
  - `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs`
  - `dart run build_runner watch --delete-conflicting-outputs`

## NEVER
- ❌ Disable lints “because annoying” — fix the cause or document the exception
- ❌ Commit code with analyzer warnings
